# Research's search accounts (docs/SERVER.md §3.7). Copy to .env.search, which is never committed.
# compose loads it into the search service and both engines; each reads only its own variables.

# The search service: the residential proxy for the paid search engine, billed per GB, as
# http://<user>:<password>_country-US@core-residential.evomi.com:1000 (not the dashboard's
# host:port:user:password). Percent-encode special characters in the password.
# Empty: the paid engine goes direct, and our IP is blocked by it.
SEARCH_PROXY_URL=

# The engines: search APIs with free monthly allowances, one key each for both bots, paced evenly
# through the month (docs/SERVER.md §9). A provider whose key is empty isn't asked.
# Tavily (https://app.tavily.com): 1,000 credits a month.
TAVILY_API_KEY=
# Exa (https://dashboard.exa.ai): $10 of credit a month.
EXA_API_KEY=
# Bright Data (https://brightdata.com/cp): 5,000 SERP requests a month, through a SERP zone
# (BRIGHTDATA_ZONE; empty: serp_api1).
BRIGHTDATA_API_KEY=
BRIGHTDATA_ZONE=
